%% figure
%% owner: the maintainer (README, Feedback)
%% source: docs/diagrams/minimal-message.mermaid (this file). Export: minimal-message.svg (docs/diagrams/exports.json)
%% question: What is the smallest complete run of the public operations, from first contact to delivery evidence, and in what order may its steps happen?
%% profile: 1 (one operator runs the RDP and the Delivery Service; no relay); verification grade; the default scope; one recipient device
%% status: current
%% references: docs/message-lifecycle.md (this figure's walkthrough); wallet-rdp-openapi.yaml; delivery-service-openapi.yaml; I-D "Message Flows and Delivery States"; docs/federated-flow-explainer.md (the four-corner version)
%% alt: Wallet A reserves and commits Wallet B's KeyPackages at the Delivery Service, deposits one Welcome per device of B and registers as the group's founder. Wallet B collects its Welcome and acknowledges it, which is joining; this may happen before or after A submits. A submits the ciphertext and metadata to the RDP, which has the Delivery Service accept the same octets before it seals the Sending Evidence and returns it. B collects the message, which marks it transferred and returns a collection token, and acknowledges with that token; the Delivery Service signs the S2 receipt. B decrypts, recomputes the digest and sends its confirmation to the RDP, which issues the Delivery Evidence dated when it verified the confirmation, and the Evidence Package to A.
%% end figure
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor A as Wallet A · sender
    participant R as Provider · RDP
    participant D as Provider · Delivery Service
    actor B as Wallet B · recipient
    Note over A,B: Profile 1 — one operator runs the RDP and the Delivery Service, so nothing is relayed
    A->>D: reserve B's KeyPackages (Idempotency-Key) and commit them — consumed from here
    A->>D: deposit one Welcome per device of B · register as the group's founder
    B->>D: collect the Welcome · acknowledge it (DELETE) — this is joining
    Note over B,D: may come before or after steps 4–7 — the open invitation already routes B's device
    A->>R: submit the ciphertext + metadata, with the sender's signature
    R->>D: the same octets
    D-->>R: acceptance record
    R-->>A: SE — sealed only after the acceptance
    B->>D: collect → transferred, with a collection token
    B->>D: acknowledge with the token
    D-->>B: signed receipt — S2, the Delivery Service's own clock
    B->>B: decrypt · recompute the digest — S3
    B->>R: confirmation (s3), wallet-signed or session-bound
    R-->>B: DE — dated when the RDP verified the confirmation
    R-->>A: Evidence Package
